---
const durable = [
  {
    name: "Contracts",
    body: "What each component promises: inputs, outputs, side effects and invariants, like “a refund never exceeds the original charge.” People own these.",
  },
  {
    name: "Evidence",
    body: "Tests, traces and benchmarks showing the promises hold. Machines produce most of it and re-run it constantly.",
  },
  {
    name: "The map",
    body: "How components relate: who calls whom, what data flows where, who owns what. Derived from the code on every change.",
  },
];
---

<section class="section wrap idea" aria-labelledby="idea-title">
  <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="idea-title">The idea</h2>
  <blockquote class="thesis">
    <p>
      Changes should be understood as shifts in meaning, scored by risk, and approved by evidence
      rather than by someone reading lines.
    </p>
  </blockquote>

  <div class="durable">
    <p class="prose durable-intro">
      Users never see your code. They see behavior, and code is becoming the cheapest way to produce
      it. So the source of truth moves to three things that outlive any version of the code. Agents can
      rewrite, regenerate or restructure the code freely, as long as the contracts hold and the evidence
      passes.
    </p>
    <dl class="durable-list">
      {
        durable.map((d) => (
          <div>
            <dt class="subhead">{d.name}</dt>
            <dd>{d.body}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .thesis {
    border-left: 8px solid var(--ink);
    padding-left: clamp(1rem, 0.5rem + 2vw, 2rem);
  }

  .thesis p {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 1rem + 3vw, 3.4rem);
    font-stretch: 108%;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    max-width: 24ch;
  }

  .durable {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 1.5rem + 3vw, 4rem);
  }

  .durable-list {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1.75rem clamp(1.5rem, 1rem + 2vw, 3rem);
  }

  dd {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 36ch;
  }
</style>
